From 2c0403404b90b0e97dcfbe16f224e927e184d812 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nano-perf-dev <nano-perf-dev@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:29:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hybrid): chunked linear cross-entropy fusion
 (cross_entropy_fusion_impl='linear')

HybridModel's output layer and cross-entropy fused over vocabulary chunks, without the fp32
copies of the logits that vocab_parallel_cross_entropy makes. Selected with
cross_entropy_loss_fusion=True and cross_entropy_fusion_impl='linear' (the name upstream's
dev branch uses for its Blackwell-only linear cross-entropy); off by default, where the
model is built and runs exactly as before.

- fusions/fused_chunked_linear_cross_entropy.py: an autograd function over vocabulary chunks.
  Forward: one GEMM per chunk and a Triton kernel reducing each row to the chunk max, sum of
  exp and target logit; the partials combine into the unfused formula
  log(sum_exp) - (target - max). Backward: each chunk's logits (kept from the forward or
  recomputed with one GEMM, per cross_entropy_fusion_saved_logit_chunks) are overwritten
  with (exp(x - max) / sum_exp - onehot) * grad_loss in fp32, rounded once (libdevice exp and
  div_rn give the same fp32 values as the unfused torch ops); grad_hidden accumulates in fp32
  across chunks; each chunk's weight-gradient rows come from one GEMM, written out or
  accumulated into main_grad as ColumnParallelLinear does under gradient-accumulation fusion.
  The upstream gradient is applied in the backward, so any per-token loss weighting is exact.
- transformer/linear_cross_entropy.py: LinearCrossEntropyModule, a ColumnParallelLinear whose
  forward returns the [b, s] per-token loss when given labels, so module hooks (the
  distributed optimizer's parameter all-gather wait) still run. The loss path refuses
  tensor-parallel vocabularies, bias, defer_embedding_wgrad_compute and cpu_offloading; the
  logits path is ColumnParallelLinear's, so a model trained with the fusion loads anywhere.
- models/hybrid/hybrid_model.py: builds it when the fusion is selected, routes labelled
  non-inference forwards through it, and refuses multi-token prediction and MuP (both need
  logits). Parameter names, shapes and checkpoint keys are unchanged.
- model_parallel_config.py: 'linear' in cross_entropy_fusion_impl, plus
  cross_entropy_fusion_vocab_chunk_size (16384) and cross_entropy_fusion_saved_logit_chunks (0).
- models/common/language_module/language_module.py: compute_language_model_loss raises for
  'linear' instead of leaving the loss unassigned.
- tensor_parallel/layers.py: the main_grad accumulation and grad_added_to_main_grad dummy-grad
  logic of LinearWithGradAccumulationAndAsyncCommunication.backward, and
  ColumnParallelLinear's weight choice, move unchanged into shared helpers.
- utils.py: drain_embedding_wgrad_compute accumulates through the same main_grad helper instead
  of its own copy of the dtype dispatch.

Applies on top of the hybrid EP-overlap port (HybridModel._postprocess comes from it).
